A||||24||Four-Banger||Your First Fiero||||12||
Z||000000||Four-Banger||04-02-2001||11:15 AM||||It's no suprise to anyone that fieros are addicting, but where did your addiction begin?  My dad gave me my fiero when I graduated high school.  It's a sweet car and turns a lot of heads, I love it!!||||reg||12
Z||000001||Rodrv6||04-02-2001||11:26 AM||||My addiction began in October, 83 when I went into a Pontiac dealer with a friend to look at a Fiero.  I spent the next week figuring out if I could afford to buy a new car and went down to the local dealer and ordered a new SE.  It was delivered in February 84 and I still have it.  Lots of fun <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||6
Z||000002||Mr.Frosty||04-02-2001||11:34 AM||||My first was an '84 silver coupe with power everything and,sunroof.I got it in '94.Did a lot of tuning to that car,and it had 130,xxx on the clock when I sold it.I put about 50,000 miles on it myself. Sweeet. Wish I never sold it now.It sucks seeing someone drive it around town sometimes with the tailpipe draggin,and,missin,and crappin.OOooohhwwwwmmmwwm.sob.sob.sob.I'm better now.<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula T-top <BR>85 GT Turbo||||reg||10
Z||000003||skitime||04-02-2001||01:59 PM||||In 87 I was looking for a project car.  From a rebuildable wreck dealer, I bought a 87 GT with only 2000 miles for 2500.  Replaced a rear quarter panel and door then repainted.  It was an awesome car that I would of never been able to afford at that time.  It was a gold GT with all options including leather interior and still under warranty.  I kept it for four years then my wife made me get rid of it.  Twenty years later I got rid of the wife and got a GT again. Life is funny. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Four-Banger||04-02-2001||02:36 PM||||Damn women!  They just don't understand cars, but you do have to be a fan of a fiero to understand the special "bond" that exists between it and the owner.  Sounds like a sweet deal you had, I would have fought like hell to keep that car.<P>Any other stories?||||reg||8
Z||000005||Kelvin Vivian||04-02-2001||02:49 PM||||Hey Four-Banger,<P>My father gave me my first Fiero too, during my junior year of college, back in 1995:<P>A white 1985 SE 2M4, had to learn to drive the 5-spd quickly as it was my summer car... I subsequently gave the car back to father as soon as I acquired my own, a 1988 GT in May 1997 (as college grad gift to myself), and 1987 SE 4-cyl (Oct 2000 as a graduate school grad gift to myself). I still love that 85, and it's also still technically mine, dad barely drives the 85.<P>Specs of first Fiero<BR>1985 SE 2M4: <BR>PL, PM, PW, cruise, rear. def, sunroof, AC, luggage rack.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1601741&a=12208700&p=44402874&Sequence=1&res=high">  88 T-top, 5-spd & 87 SE 4-cyl, 5-spd||||reg||1
Z||000006||skitime||04-02-2001||02:54 PM||||Hey Kelvin,  The car I have now is identical to your 88 t-top.  Yours looks great.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Pontiaddict||04-02-2001||04:49 PM||||I also got my first Fiero from my dad. He traded a motorcycle for it. It was a 84 4 speed (econo) with minimal options. I liked the car, but I was looking for a little more power out of the duke. When a friend backed into it, I decided to sell it and get an 85 GT that needed some work. I never did get that car. Now I just regret selling it because it would have made a great v8 car.||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroLisa||04-02-2001||05:09 PM||||Four Banger- hey now, not all women don't respect cars!<P>I got my first Fiero when I was 15, but for my 16th b-day. It was an '86 gold coupe, no options. Spent 2 years restoring it. Just sold that car in January to pay for the new GT.||||reg||1
Z||000009||btoth||04-02-2001||05:58 PM||||My first car was an '87 Coupe.  Only paid $700 for it and I knew the girl that I bought it from.  She didn't want it because she didn't like trying to get in and out of it.  I had always wanted a Fiero, 300zx, or RX-7 and I couldn't pass up the price.  The car ran perfect after the new alternator and was so much fun to drive.  Unfortunatly, the summer after I graduated from high school some moron tried to pass me while I was making a left-hand turn and took off my front end.  (He was an officer in training and didn't even know who to call.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> And he was doing about 60mph in a 45 zone too!)  I had only had the car for 6 months and needed to have another Fiero so I bought my current '86 GT from a guy my dad worked with.||||reg||7
Z||000010||TheFiero64||04-02-2001||05:59 PM||||I drove my Girlfriend's 84 SE and have been hooked ever since.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000011||Bluebottlejunky||04-02-2001||08:32 PM||||Well I just got my first fiero this last month an 85 GT 4sp..im only 15 1/2 right now but that just gives me time to enjoy it and fix it up.  I first started to like Fiero's in 1993 when I was 6, my sister brought home a new boyfreind who had a Black 86 V-6 SE T-top, from the second that he poped open the deck lid and I saw the engine was in the back my jaw drop to the ground and I new I had to have one. Im so glad they got married  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> or....maybe it was the riding in the Fiero at night with those orange glowing lights for the guages?<P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85' GT 4sp||||reg||1
Z||000012||danny boy||04-02-2001||08:35 PM|||| My first was an 86 base coupe 5sp. Got it for graduation(how ironic). I hated it at first because I went from a 1970 Nova SS with 410 dyno'd rear wheel HP to a POS 4cyl. Little did I know....||||reg||7
Z||000013||Tina||04-03-2001||01:23 AM||||This is, how I got mine.<P>Telephone rings.<BR>Boyfriend: Hey Tina, do you want a new car?<BR>Me: YES<BR>Boyfriend: But,it's not a german car.<BR>Me:That's, o.k.<BR>Boyfriend: But it's red.<BR>Me: I can live with red.<BR>Boyfriend: But it only has two seats.<BR>Me:  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I'll take it.<BR>Boyfriend: Did I mention it has no engine?<BR>Me:Minor detail  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>The rest is history.||||reg||1
Z||000014||DavidHenshaw||04-03-2001||02:35 PM||||I knew nothing about Fieros until the summer of 2000. I didn't even know they existed. Yes I live in America etc, etc. <P>Then one fateful day I looked at a sight on the net comparing the relative performance of Mr2's, RX 7's, Honda CRX's and Fieros. Anyway the Fiero was best in the six cylinder iteration. So I start looking and couldn't believe how beautiful the car was. I mean it makes the other three look like a bad haircut. Ended up buying a white 86 GT v6 in pretty good shape and love it. These cars are special.<P>Dave<P>BTW when I get done my baby is going to be beautiful.||||reg||1
Z||000015||mbramble||04-03-2001||02:55 PM||||I had never heard of a Fiero until my daughter bought an 87 basic coupe in '93.  We were out of the country (in the Navy) during the production years of the Fiero.  Anyway, she drove it until she got married and moved away. My second oldest son bought it from her and drove it until he went into the Navy and then decided he wanted something newer for driving across country.  He owed me a couple hundred dollars and asked if I'd take the car instead.  I did, though I didn't really care to have it.  Just more convenient for it to be in my name when I decided to sell it.  It ran like absolute crap.  Decided to keep it so my youngest could drive it when he got a license. Had some work done at the Pontiac dealer (new coil pack) and it has run great every since.  Just about the time I fell in love with it, he got his license and school started and he began driving it everyday.  I get to drive it on the weekends occassionally.  I just bought an 85 GT project car and once he leaves for college, the doors, headlight motors, etc., will come off the coupe and go on the GT.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Raydar||04-03-2001||04:31 PM||||My first Fiero was a white 85 GT that I bought new. Traded it on an 88 (POS) Firebird Formula -two weeks before they cancelled the Fiero. DOH!  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000017||Four-Banger||04-03-2001||10:57 PM||||Lisa, I am a girl, that's how I know that girl's don't always appreciate cars.  A lot of the time, I'm right there with pop or the bf swearing at bushings and unknown rattles.  Plus, I'm very jealous of the bf's car.  It's his second car, his first was a station wagon.  Sometimes, he talks about his car so much, I think it's a person and it talks back to him.  He's been wanting to call it Knight Rider, but I'm refusing this name and call it the *****  Mobile since the wagon was the Bat Mobile.  He gets really upset when I call it the *****  Mobile, but I get upset and jealous when he can spend an hour telling me how nice his car looks and what he's done to it, when he can't take a few seconds and tell me how nice I look.  I don't blame him a bit for talking so much about his car, but I think he forgets that I'm his girlfriend and not his buddy.  I need to go get him, so he can get on my computer and look at fiero stuff.  ||||reg||4
Z||000018||qwikgta||04-03-2001||11:53 PM||||July 1983, POCI convention in Buffalo, NY.  GM brings two Fieros, a fully optioned coupe and one with no body panels on it, it is stripped bare.  Im 17 y.o. and driving a 1976 trans am, i sit in this "new car" that Pontiac is making, and Im in love.  I read everything about it, my uncle works at a dealership and he gets me all the latest info.  I cant wait to get one.  Well, I go off and join the Navy and my driving days are few and far between.  Finally in 88 i find a 87 GT for sale at a local lot.  I buy it and I have been hooked on them ever since.  I have two now and i am always looking for more.  You guys are the only ones who understand the feeling of seeing one on the road and woundering if the person driving is a ally or just some idiot driving the poor thing into the dirt.  I hope we keep this forum and the little fiero alive forever.  Thanks<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>QWIKGTA<BR>88 T-Top coupe<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||1
Z||000019||Jaygee79||04-04-2001||12:20 AM||||Won mine right before I got my license.  Had it ever since.  It got Josh hooked once he drove it   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Four-Banger, I can sympathize with your bf.  I sometimes talk to my car.  I even say good night to her when I get home from work  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Jaygee79 (edited 04-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||Four-Banger||04-04-2001||02:20 PM||||okay,those stars mean B*tch Mobile.  Sorry about all those.||||reg||11
Z||000021||FieroLisa||04-04-2001||03:30 PM||||Four Banger - first of all, *yay* for more girls  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>as for the boyfriend...some guys I've dated, the car has been more reliable! Sorry to hear about him being so obsessed with his car...but ya better set him straight that you are much more important!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000022||rforbes||04-04-2001||04:42 PM||||Got my first fiero just a few months ago.  '84 sport coupe, sunroof, power windows, ...  It looks a little rough because it sat outside quite a while before I bought it.  It had a hole in one piston.  I rebuilt the engine and it hums along pretty well now.  I still need a paint job and some interior work but overall not a bad ride now.  I was hooked on Fieros when they fist came out and in '86 we (wife and I) almost bought one.  I was in the Navy at the time and young so had conserns about insurance on a 20 year old driving a sporst car.  About two weeks after we passed on this car, we found out there would be a new addition to the family in a few months so..  probably a two-seater is not the right car for a family of three.  Now 15 years later my son is anxious to get his turn behind the wheel of his (MY) dream car.  My 11 year old daughter is also wanting a turn in a few years.  I guess I might have to invest in AT LEAST 1 more Fiero before it's all over.<P>BTW I am in central Missouri and haven't seen anyone else on the forum in this area.  Are there any around Columbia??||||reg||10
Z||000023||mark's 86||04-04-2001||08:20 PM||||I got my first fiero when I turned 17 it was a basic ffour banger with the throttle body that somehow caught fire. My second fiero didnt come until I turned 23 it is a 86gt fastback. I love it ||||reg||10
Z||000024||Four-Banger||04-05-2001||02:45 PM||||He knows, he just not a very expressive person.  As for me, I'm outgoing and you can't get me to shut-up once I've started talking.  The car is his hobby, I'm his woman, and he said just being my better half is a full-time job.  Don't worry, I tease him about his car and he gets plenty bitter.  Ever heard "Piece of Sh*t Car" by Adam Sandler?  I sing that to him.||||reg||6
